<p>The item is a big box. Someone tried to open it once, and a bad traffic accident happened nearby. Now there is a ghost car from that accident&#8230;<br />
Nope, I don't like it.</p>
<p>First, you need more on the container. One accident is a coincidence; if there is a disaster every time they try to open it, move it, x-ray it, what have you, then you've got something anomalous.<br />
Second, there is no connection between the box and the ghost car. Why that Ford and not the other flaming wrecks? There doesn't need to be a conclusive forensic trail, but we poor readers need at least a hint of a connection, even if it's just fridge logic.</p>

